# Build context exclusions. The Dockerfile's build stage does `COPY . .`, so
# anything not listed here is uploaded to the daemon and lands in a build
# layer. Two of those things must never be there: the SQLite ledger under
# data/, and the .env files holding SESSION_SECRET and mail credentials.
#
# The final image is multi-stage and only copies dist/, web/dist/ and
# migrations/, so today none of this reaches the shipped image - but the build
# layers and the local builder cache still hold whatever the context carried,
# and a future single-stage build or a CI job pushing to a public registry
# would publish it. Keep the context clean instead of relying on that.
#
# Do NOT add scripts/ here: tsconfig.json compiles scripts/**/*.ts, so
# `yarn build:api` needs it.

# --- Secrets ---
.env*
!.env.example
!.env.prod.example
!.env.deploy.example
# Local telemetry, injected by deploy.sh into web/public/telemetry.js on the
# host *before* docker build, so the build never needs this file itself.
.telemetry.js
*.pem
*.key
id_rsa*

# --- The ledger. Never in an image layer. ---
data/
**/*.db
**/*.db-wal
**/*.db-shm

# Raw Splitwise export snapshots: personal financial data.
splitwise-export/

# --- Dependencies and build output ---
# node_modules must be excluded for correctness as well as size: `COPY . .`
# runs after `yarn install`, so a host tree would overwrite the freshly
# installed one and drop darwin-arm64 better-sqlite3 bindings into a
# linux/amd64 image.
node_modules/
dist/
web/dist/

# --- Test artifacts and images ---
smoke/runs/
smoke/baselines/
# Image tars written by scripts/deploy/deploy.sh; without this, each build's
# context would carry the previous build's image.
**/*.tar

# --- Local noise ---
.git/
.gitignore
.claude/
.cursor/
.DS_Store
**/*.log
**/*.swp
